<title>UK: IEA supply/demand highlights - end February report.</title>
<headline>IEA supply/demand highlights - end February report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table highlights the oil supply-demand and stock estimates included in the International Energy Agency's latest Monthly Oil Market Report.</p>
<p>Figures in million barrels per day.</p>
<p>		  1994 1995 1Q96 2Q96 3Q96 4Q96 1996 1Q97 2Q97 3Q97 4Q97 1997</p>
<p>DEMAND</p>
<p> OECD	   40.0 40.4 42.1 39.6 40.7 42.2 41.1 42.5 40.3 41.3 42.9 41.8</p>
<p> NON-OECD     28.9 29.9 31.0 30.2 30.2 31.5 30.7 32.1 31.4 31.3 33.2 32.0</p>
<p> TOTAL	  68.9 70.2 73.1 69.8 70.9 73.6 71.9 74.6 71.7 72.6 76.1 73.7</p>
<p>SUPPLY</p>
<p> NON-OPEC     41.6 42.4 43.3 43.2 43.3 44.3 43.6 44.9 44.6 45.2 47.0 45.4</p>
<p> OPEC CRUDE   24.7 25.1 25.7 25.6 25.9 26.3 25.9</p>
<p> OPEC NGLS     2.4  2.4  2.5  2.6  2.7  2.7  2.6  2.8  2.8  2.9  3.0  2.9</p>
<p> TOTAL OPEC   27.0 27.5 28.2 28.2 28.6 29.0 28.5</p>
<p> TOTAL SUPPLY 68.6 69.9 71.5 71.4 72.0 73.2 72.0</p>
<p> OPEC CALL*   24.9 25.4 27.3 24.0 24.9 26.7 25.7 26.8 24.2 24.5 26.1 25.4</p>
<p> IND STOCKS   +0.1 -0.3 -1.3 +1.2 +0.5 -0.5 +0.0</p>
<p> TOT STCK BAL -0.3 -0.1 -1.6  1.6 +1.1 -0.4 +0.2</p>
<p> FSU NET EXP   2.4  2.4  2.4  2.8  2.8  2.9  2.7  2.7  2.9  2.9 2.7 2.8</p>
<p>* Implied call on OPEC crude equals total demand minus total non-OPEC supply minus OPEC NGLs. Thus includes &quot;miscellaneous to balance&quot; for historical time periods.</p>
